.TH EWM 1 ewm\-VERSION
.SH NAME
ewm \- Epsilons window manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ewm
.RB [ \-v ]
.br
.B ewm-msg
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR path ]
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ewm is a tiling window manager for X, forked from dwm. It manages windows in
tiled, monocle and floating layouts, plus any layout written in Lua. Windows
are grouped by tags; selecting tags displays the windows with these tags.
.P
Each screen has a bar showing the tags, the layout, the title of the focused
window and, on the focused screen, the status text (the X root window name,
set with
.BR xsetroot (1),
or
.BR ewm.setstatus ).
The tags of the focused window are
marked with a filled square, occupied tags with an empty one. A floating
window has an empty square before its title.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
prints version information to stderr, then exits.
.SH CONFIGURATION
ewm is configured in Lua (5.3 or newer) through
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ewm/config.lua
(default
.BR ~/.config/ewm/config.lua ),
or
.B $EWM_CONFIG
if set. On the first start it is created from the installed default,
.BR PREFIX/share/ewm/config.lua .
Example plugins are installed in
.BR PREFIX/share/ewm/examples .
.P
Afterwards every
.B *.lua
file in the
.B plugins
directory next to config.lua is run in name order. Modules next to config.lua
can be loaded with
.BR require ,
compiled Lua modules
.RB ( *.so )
included. When no configuration can be loaded ewm starts with built-in
defaults: Mod4\-Return opens
.B $TERMINAL
(or xterm), Mod4\-[1..9] views tags, Mod4\-Shift\-r restarts and
Mod4\-Shift\-e quits.
.P
ewm watches these directories and reloads the configuration when a
.B .lua
file changes. A reload runs the configuration in a new Lua state; only if it
loads without errors does it replace the running one, otherwise the error is
shown in the bar and the previous configuration stays active. Values like
mfact or gappx that were changed at runtime are kept unless the configured
value changed.
.SS The ewm module
.TP
.BI ewm.set{ key " = " value ", ...}"
Settings:
.BR borderpx ,
.BR snap ,
.BR gappx ,
.B gapmodes
(list of gap sizes cycled by switchgaps),
.BR showbar ,
.BR topbar ,
.B barpadding
(extra bar height),
.BR mfact ,
.BR nmaster ,
.BR resizehints ,
.BR autoreload ,
.B fonts
(list of fontconfig names),
.B colors
.RB ( {norm={fg,bg,border},\ sel={fg,bg,border}} ),
.B tags
(list of up to 31 names),
.B layouts
(names in order; the first is the default, unlisted ones follow).
.TP
.BI ewm.key( mods ", " key ", " fn ", " args... )
Call
.IR fn ( args... )
when
.I key
(a keysym name, see
.BR xev (1))
is pressed with the modifiers
.I mods
("Mod4+Shift", "" or a list; Shift, Control, Mod1\-Mod5, Alt, Super).
.TP
.BI ewm.button( click ", " mods ", " button ", " fn ", " args... )
Mouse bindings.
.I click
is one of tagbar, layout, status, title, client or root. A tagbar binding
without arguments receives the clicked tag number.
.TP
.BI ewm.rule{class=, instance=, title=, tags=, floating=, monitor=}
Applied to new windows whose properties contain the given strings.
.TP
.BI ewm.layout( name ", " symbol ", " fn )
Define a layout.
.IR fn ( area ", " n )
gets the window area
.RB ( x ,
.BR y ,
.BR w ,
.BR h ,
.BR gap ,
.BR mfact ,
.BR nmaster ,
.BR monitor )
and the number of tiled windows, and returns a list of
.B {x, y, w, h}
boxes (borders included), one per window in stacking order.
.TP
.BI ewm.on( event ", " fn )
Hooks: startup, manage, unmanage and focus. The latter three receive a client
table (focus may receive nil).
.TP
.BI ewm.timer( seconds ", " fn "[, " repeat "])"
Run
.I fn
after
.IR seconds ;
returns an id for
.BI ewm.cancel( id ) .
.TP
.B ewm.clients(), ewm.focused(), ewm.monitor()
Client tables have the fields id, name, class, instance, tags, floating,
fullscreen, urgent, monitor, x, y, w and h. The monitor table has num, x, y,
w, h, tags, layout, mfact and nmaster.
.TP
.BI ewm.client.focus( id "), .kill(" id "), .settags(" id ", " tags "),"
.BI .setfloating( id ", " bool "), .setfullscreen(" id ", " bool )
Act on a specific client.
.TP
.BI ewm.setstatus( text )
Show
.I text
until the root window name changes.
.TP
Actions
.BR ewm.spawn ( cmd )
(a shell command string or an argv list),
.BR ewm.view ,
.BR ewm.toggleview ,
.BR ewm.tag ,
.BR ewm.toggletag
(a tag number, a list of numbers or "all"; view without argument returns to
the previous tags),
.BR ewm.focusstack ,
.BR ewm.incnmaster ,
.BR ewm.focusmon ,
.BR ewm.tagmon ,
.BR ewm.setgaps ,
.BR ewm.switchgaps
(a number),
.BR ewm.setmfact
(a delta, or 1 + the absolute value),
.BR ewm.setlayout
(a name; none toggles the previous layout),
.BR ewm.moveresize
("dx dy dw dh" with x/y/w/h suffixes; uppercase for absolute values),
.BR ewm.moveresizeedge
(t, b, l, r moves floating windows to an edge; T, B, L, R grows them),
.BR ewm.zoom ,
.BR ewm.killclient ,
.BR ewm.togglefloating ,
.BR ewm.togglefullscreen ,
.BR ewm.togglebar ,
.BR ewm.movemouse ,
.BR ewm.resizemouse ,
.BR ewm.reload ,
.B ewm.restart
(exec the installed ewm again in place: windows, tags, layouts and focus are
kept, autostart does not run again) and
.BR ewm.quit .
.TP
.BI ewm.autostart( cmd )
Run
.I cmd
(like
.BR ewm.spawn )
once when ewm starts; ignored when the configuration is reloaded.
.TP
.B ewm.version, ewm.configdir
The version and the directory of the loaded config.lua.
.SH IPC
ewm listens on a UNIX socket, by default
.B $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ewm\-$DISPLAY.sock
(or
.BR /tmp/ewm\-$UID\-$DISPLAY.sock ),
and exports its path as
.B $EWM_SOCKET
to the programs it starts. The protocol is the one of the dwm-ipc patch.
.B ewm\-msg
talks to it:
.TP
.B ewm-msg get_monitors | get_tags | get_layouts | get_dwm_client \fIid
Print state as JSON.
.TP
.B ewm-msg run_command \fIcommand \fR[\fIargs\fR]
Run view, toggleview, tag, toggletag (tag masks), tagmon, focusmon,
focusstack, incnmaster, zoom, killclient, togglefloating, setmfact,
setlayoutsafe (a layout address from get_layouts), reload, restart or quit.
.TP
.B ewm-msg subscribe \fIevent\fR...
Print tag_change_event, client_focus_change_event, layout_change_event,
monitor_focus_change_event, focused_title_change_event and
focused_state_change_event as they happen.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EWM_CONFIG
Configuration file to load instead of the default locations.
.TP
.B EWM_SOCKET
Socket used by ewm\-msg.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dmenu (1),
.BR xsetroot (1)
.SH ISSUES
Java applications which use the XToolkit/XAWT backend may draw grey windows
only. Setting the environment variable
.B _JAVA_AWT_WM_NONREPARENTING=1
or running
.B wmname LG3D
works around this.
